          ],
          "text": "Your child was admitted at 6 hours of age. They had:\n- grunting\n- fast breathing\n- a temperature\n\nThe team found your child had neonatal sepsis. This was the main reason for their stay."
        },
        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.1",
          "heading": "what_we_did",
          "source_ids": [
            "sections.2",
            "sections.3"
          ],
          "text": "The team did a sepsis screen. This included:\n- blood tests\n- a blood culture\n- a CRP blood test\n\nA lumbar puncture was not done, as your child was stable.\n\nThe blood culture showed no growth at 36 hours and was confirmed negative at 48 hours. The CRP level rose at first, then fell on day 2.\n\nYour child was given two intravenous (IV) antibiotics:\n- benzylpenicillin\n- gentamicin\n\nThe team decided to complete a 5-day course of IV antibiotics. The course was completed on day 5.\n\nRoutine newborn checks were done. Your child passed the newborn hearing screen."
